:"Benyou","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Benyou","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Donghao","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Donghao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"liomapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Qiuchi","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Qiuchi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Zhang","key":"pengpau","last":"Peng","name":"Peng, Zhang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-aba68184-23db-4e7f-8e85-841fb846282f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"ENCODING WORD ORDER IN COMPLEX EMBEDDINGS","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-495950","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This report describes the participation of two Danish universities, University of Copenhagen and Aalborg University, in the international search engine competition on COVID-19 (the 2020 TREC-COVID Challenge) organised by the U.S. National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) and its Text Retrieval Conference (TREC) division. The aim of the competition was to find the best search engine strategy for retrieving precise biomedical scientific information on COVID-19 from the largest, at that point in time, dataset of curated scientific literature on COVID-19—the COVID-19 Open Research Dataset (CORD-19). CORD-19 was the result of a call to action to the tech community by the U.S. White House in March 2020, and was shortly thereafter posted on Kaggle as an AI competition by the Allen Institute for AI, the Chan Zuckerberg Initiative, Georgetown University’s Center for Security and Emerging Technology, Microsoft, and the National Library of Medicine at the US National Institutes of Health. CORD-19 contained over 200,000 scholarly articles (of which more than 100,000 were with full text) about COVID-19, SARS-CoV-2, and related coronaviruses, gathered from curated biomedical sources. The TRECCOVID challenge asked for the best way to (a) retrieve accurate and precise scientific information, in response to some queries formulated by biomedical experts, and (b) rank this information decreasingly by its relevance to the query. In this document, we describe the TREC-COVID competition setup, our participation to it, and our resulting reflections and lessons learned about the state-of-art technology when faced with the acute task of retrieving precise scientific information from a rapidly growing corpus of literature, in response to highly specialised queries, in the middle of a pandemic.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Lima, Lucas Chaves","Hansen, Casper","Hansen, Christian","Wang, Dongsheng","Maistro, Maria","Larsen, Birger","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Lioma, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-081965"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Covid 19","Information retrieval"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"denmark s participation in the search engine trec covid 000000000019 challenge lessons learned about searching for precise biomedical scientific information on covid 000000000019","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"doo","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.12684v2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-081965","ids":["aau-6dc9bff5-5301-49d1-a240-b243df8e8e2c"],"keyword":["CORD-19","COVID-19","Information Retrieval","TREC COVID-19"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-EA2C29E110B86DA451106D896BE02F38"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.12684v2","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2011.12684.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Human Centered Science and Digital Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Purposeful Technology Lab","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Responsible Impact","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lucas Chaves","key":"limalucaschavespau","last":"Lima","name":"Lima, Lucas Chaves","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Casper","key":"hansencasperpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Casper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"hansenchristianpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dongsheng","key":"wangdongshengpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Dongsheng","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"maistromariapau","last":"Maistro","name":"Maistro, Maria","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birger","key":"larsenbirgerpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9cb12135-a825-43ba-87e2-b71651b91939","name":"Larsen, Birger","orcid":"0000-0002-3622-2698","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenjakobgruepau","last":"Simonsen","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"liomachristinapau","last":"Lioma","name":"Lioma, Christina","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"arXiv","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6dc9bff5-5301-49d1-a240-b243df8e8e2c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Denmark's Participation in the Search Engine TREC COVID-19 Challenge : Lessons Learned about Searching for Precise Biomedical Scientific Information on COVID-19","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-081965","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Recent developments in machine learning have introduced models that approach human performance at the cost of increased architectural complexity. Efforts to make the rationales behind the models’ predictions transparent have inspired an abundance of new explainability techniques. Provided with an already trained model, they compute saliency scores for the words of an input instance. However, there exists no definitive guide on (i) how to choose such a technique given a particular application task and model architecture, and (ii) the benefits and drawbacks of using each such technique. In this paper, we develop a comprehensive list of diagnostic properties for evaluating existing explainability techniques. We then employ the proposed list to compare a set of diverse explainability techniques on downstream text classification tasks and neural network architectures. We also compare the saliency scores assigned by the explainability techniques with human annotations of salient input regions to find relations between a model’s performance and the agreement of its rationales with human ones. Overall, we find that the gradient-based explanations perform best across tasks and model architectures, and we present further insights into the properties of the reviewed explainability techniques.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Atanasova, Pepa","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Lioma, Christina","Augenstein, Isabelle"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-511609"],"event":{"acronym":"EMNLP","end":"2020-11-20","place":"online","start":"2020-11-16","title":"The 2020 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a diagnostic study of explainability techniques for text classification","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2020.emnlp-main.263","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-511609","identifier":[{"id":"85104355822","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-c5f4dd32-205a-45d1-bde4-7407d3827dd7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-6DA30A0532944B27975BCD88B65BD61E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/254783377/A_Diagnostic_Study_of_Explainability_Techniques_for_Text_Classification.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2020.emnlp-main.263","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Pepa","key":"atanasovapau","last":"Atanasova","locid":"876ac9d6-217c-4e63-9e65-8f010272dce2","name":"Atanasova, Pepa","orcid":"0000-0002-0023-2616","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"liomapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Isabelle","key":"augensteinpau","last":"Augenstein","locid":"929ec255-2eae-4e6d-b826-5e7abd210f06","name":"Augenstein, Isabelle","orcid":"0000-0003-1562-7909","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2020.emnlp-main.263","pages":"3256-3274","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2020 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104355822"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c5f4dd32-205a-45d1-bde4-7407d3827dd7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Diagnostic Study of Explainability Techniques for Text Classification","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-511609","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Most existing work on automated fact checking is concerned with predicting the veracity of claims based on metadata, social network spread, language used in claims, and, more recently, evidence supporting or denying claims. A crucial piece of the puzzle that is still missing is to understand how to automate the most elaborate part of the process – generating justifications for verdicts on claims. This paper provides the first study of how these explanations can be generated automatically based on available claim context, and how this task can be modelled jointly with veracity prediction. Our results indicate that optimising both objectives at the same time, rather than training them separately, improves the performance of a fact checking system. The results of a manual evaluation further suggest that the informativeness, coverage and overall quality of the generated explanations are also improved in the multi-task model.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Atanasova, Pepa","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Lioma, Christina","Augenstein, Isabelle"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-526403"],"event":{"acronym":"ACL","end":"2020-07-10","place":"Online","start":"2020-07-05","title":"58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"generating fact checking explanations","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2020.acl-main.656","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-526403","identifier":[{"id":"85117937854","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-de955ada-20ac-426c-8c10-771979ce333e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-4F200A9F0334D54558A9DF46A843223C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/254776317/Generating_Fact_Checking_Explanations.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2020.acl-main.656","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Image Analysis, Computational Modelling and Geometry","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Pepa","key":"atanasovapau","last":"Atanasova","locid":"876ac9d6-217c-4e63-9e65-8f010272dce2","name":"Atanasova, Pepa","orcid":"0000-0002-0023-2616","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"liomapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Isabelle","key":"augensteinpau","last":"Augenstein","locid":"929ec255-2eae-4e6d-b826-5e7abd210f06","name":"Augenstein, Isabelle","orcid":"0000-0003-1562-7909","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2020.acl-main.656","pages":"7352-7364","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":": Proceedings of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117937854"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-de955ada-20ac-426c-8c10-771979ce333e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Generating Fact Checking Explanations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-526403","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"It is well-known that for infinitely repeated games, there are computable strategies that have best responses, but no computable best responses. These results were originally proved for either specific games (e.g., Prisoner's dilemma), or for classes of games satisfying certain conditions not known to be both necessary and sufficient. We derive a complete characterization in the form of simple necessary and sufficient conditions for the existence of a computable strategy without a computable best response under limit-of-means payoff. We further refine the characterization by requiring the strategy profiles to be Nash equilibria or subgame-perfect equilibria, and we show how the characterizations entail that it is efficiently decidable whether an infinitely repeated game has a computable strategy without a computable best response. Full version: https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.13921","author_count":2,"contributors":["Dargaj, Jakub","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-528159"],"event":{"end":"2020-07-17","place":"Virtual, Online, hu","start":"2020-07-13","title":"21st ACM Conference on Economics and Computation, EC 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a complete characterization of infinitely repeated two player games having computable strategies with no computable best response under limit of means payoff","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3391403.3399520","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-528159","identifier":[{"id":"85089280150","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e1725c63-0efd-4997-9837-1fa0bff62d09"],"keyword":["computable strategy","repeated game","subgame-perfect equilibrium"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1F8ED673F69B3F27601C99C08D60EFBF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3391403.3399520","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/260413493/A_Complete_Characterization_of_Infinitely_Repeated.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jakub","key":"dargajpau","last":"Dargaj","locid":"b9f222a8-f7ab-440e-ad22-f95ed1d81797","name":"Dargaj, Jakub","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3391403.3399520","eisbn":["9781450379755"],"pages":"69-70","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"EC 2020 - Proceedings of the 21st ACM Conference on Economics and Computation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089280150"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e1725c63-0efd-4997-9837-1fa0bff62d09"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Complete Characterization of Infinitely Repeated Two-Player Games having Computable Strategies with no Computable Best Response under Limit-of-Means Payoff","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-528159","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Programming language concepts are used to give some new perspectives on a long-standing open problem: is LOGSPACE = PTIME ?.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jones, Neil","Bhaskar, Siddharth","Kop, Cynthia","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-405421"],"event":{"end":"2020-04-26","place":"Dublin, ie","start":"2020-04-25","title":"8th International Workshop on Verification and Program Transformation, VPT 2020 and 7th Workshop on Horn Clauses for Verification and Synthesis, HCVS 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cons free programs and complexity classes between logspace and ptime","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.320.5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-405421","identifier":[{"id":"85091988483","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-141c58ae-98db-4587-a148-bd9155b73792"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7EE4E70E2E48185C13CE0765E4058942"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2008.02932v1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.320.5","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Neil D.","key":"jonespau","last":"Jones","locid":"d75098fb-0869-4abd-bb9f-6fae75c7296c","name":"Jones, Neil","name_org":"Jones, Neil D.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Siddharth","key":"bhaskarpau","last":"Bhaskar","locid":"c3fa456a-4a94-4d42-8069-80f42894cec1","name":"Bhaskar, Siddharth","orcid":"0000-0003-4157-8768","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Cynthia","key":"koppau","last":"Kop","name":"Kop, Cynthia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4204/eptcs.320.5","issn":["20752180"],"journal":"Electronic Proceedings in Theoretical Computer Science","pages":"65-79","status":"p","title":"Electronic Proceedings in Theoretical Computer Science","volume":"320"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091988483"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-141c58ae-98db-4587-a148-bd9155b73792"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cons-free programs and complexity classes between LOGSPACE and PTIME","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-405421","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Semantic Hashing is a popular family of methods for efficient similarity search in large-scale datasets. In Semantic Hashing, documents are encoded as short binary vectors (i.e., hash codes), such that semantic similarity can be efficiently computed using the Hamming distance. Recent state-of-the-art approaches have utilized weak supervision to train better performing hashing models. Inspired by this, we present Semantic Hashing with Pairwise Reconstruction (PairRec), which is a discrete variational autoencoder based hashing model. PairRec first encodes weakly supervised training pairs (a query document and a semantically similar document) into two hash codes, and then learns to reconstruct the same query document from both of these hash codes (i.e., pairwise reconstruction). This pairwise reconstruction enables our model to encode local neighbourhood structures within the hash code directly through the decoder. We experimentally compare PairRec to traditional and state-of-the-art approaches, and obtain significant performance improvements in the task of document similarity search.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hansen, Casper","Hansen, Christian","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Alstrup, Stephen","Lioma, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-522480"],"event":{"acronym":"SIGIR","end":"2020-07-30","place":"Virtual, Online, cn","start":"2020-07-25","title":"43rd Annual International ACM SIGIR Conference on Research and Development in Information Retrieval, SIGIR 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Semantic hashing","Variational"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unsupervised semantic hashing with pairwise reconstruction","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3397271.3401220","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-522480","identifier":[{"id":"85090121707","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d8079968-f1d5-40ae-8372-e0ed073522ca"],"keyword":["pairwise reconstruction","semantic hashing","variational"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-49005F97A1005A4AE6DF68EEFE6B357F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3397271.3401220","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/260411533/Unsupervised_Semantic_Hashing_with_Pairwise_Reconstruction.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Casper","key":"hansencasperpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"0f5313ce-6e55-41ec-88c7-8368f583f459","name":"Hansen, Casper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hansenchristianpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"58729b14-2de9-4102-91e9-8d2bc16b539e","name":"Hansen, Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenjakobgruepau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stephen","key":"alstrupstephenpau","last":"Alstrup","locid":"6d1b63fb-235a-4932-8345-413b4ac8d6a5","name":"Alstrup, Stephen","orcid":"0000-0001-7896-8386","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"liomachristinapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3397271.3401220","eisbn":["9781450380164"],"pages":"2009-2012","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"SIGIR 2020 - Proceedings of the 43rd International ACM SIGIR Conference on Research and Development in Information Retrieval"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090121707"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d8079968-f1d5-40ae-8372-e0ed073522ca"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Unsupervised Semantic Hashing with Pairwise Reconstruction","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-522480","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"We study the computational complexity of uniformly converting the base-a expansion of an irrational numbers to the base-b expansion. In particular, we are interested in subsets of the irrationals where such conversion can be performed with little overhead. We show that such conversion is possible, essentially with polynomial overhead, for the set of irrationals that are not Liouville numbers. Furthermore, it is known that there are irrational numbers x such that the expansion of x in one integer base is efficiently computable, but the expansion of x in certain other integer bases is not. We prove that any such number must be a Liouville number.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jakobsen, Sune Kristian","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-527940"],"event":{"acronym":"CIE","end":"2020-07-03","place":"Fisciano, it","start":"2020-06-29","title":"16th Conference on Computability in Europe, CiE 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computability","Computational complexity","Diophantine approximation","Number theory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"liouville numbers and the computational complexity of changing bases","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-51466-2_5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-527940","identifier":[{"id":"85088208927","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e11a44b1-e741-46bd-8a55-5868f1e7cefc"],"keyword":["Computability","Computational complexity","Diophantine approximation","Number theory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A2AD526E6280E611377766CB5622A278"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-51466-2_5","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Sune Kristian","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"a1436d6d-14c7-43f5-9246-50cc4ac03296","name":"Jakobsen, Sune Kristian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marcella","key":"anselmopedh","last":"Anselmo","name":"Anselmo, Marcella","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gianluca","key":"dellavedovapedh","last":"Della Vedova","name":"Della Vedova, Gianluca","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Florin","key":"maneapedh","last":"Manea","name":"Manea, Florin","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Arno","key":"paulypedh","last":"Pauly","name":"Pauly, Arno","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-51466-2_5","isbn":["9783030514655"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"50-62","publisher":"Springer VS","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Beyond the Horizon of Computability - 16th Conference on Computability in Europe, CiE 2020, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088208927"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e11a44b1-e741-46bd-8a55-5868f1e7cefc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Liouville Numbers and the Computational Complexity of Changing Bases","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-527940","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"It is known that while it is possible to convert between many different representations of irrational numbers (e.g., between Dedekind cuts and Cauchy sequences), it is in general not possible to do so subrecursively: conversions in general need to perform unbounded search. This raises the question of categorizing the pairs of representations between which either subrecursive conversion is possible, or is not possible. The purpose of this paper is to prove the following positive result: for a number of well-known representations (Beatty sequences, Dedekind cuts, General base expansions, Hurwitz characteristics, and Locators) conversion between the representations can be performed effectively and with good subrecursive bounds.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Kristiansen, Lars","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-488919"],"event":{"acronym":"CIE","end":"2020-07-03","place":"Fisciano, it","start":"2020-06-29","title":"16th Conference on Computability in Europe, CiE 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computational complexity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the complexity of conversion between classic real number representations","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85088210085&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-488919","identifier":[{"id":"85088210085","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9fba6130-2c02-44e4-9c2b-e3cba86ba75d"],"keyword":["Computable analysis","Computational complexity","Representation of irrational numbers","Subrecursion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Globa