":"Casper","key":"hansencasperpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"0f5313ce-6e55-41ec-88c7-8368f583f459","name":"Hansen, Casper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stephen","key":"alstrupstephenpau","last":"Alstrup","locid":"6d1b63fb-235a-4932-8345-413b4ac8d6a5","name":"Alstrup, Stephen","orcid":"0000-0001-7896-8386","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenjakobgruepau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"liomachristinapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781450359405"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"WSDM '19: Proceedings of the Twelfth ACM International Conference on Web Search and Data Mining"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8a983feb-a0f2-4b48-ad8d-7f9b2866e596"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modelling Sequential Music Track Skips using a Multi-RNN Approach","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-476290","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Classic results in computability theory concern extensional results: the behaviour of partial recursive functions rather than the programs computing them. We prove a generalisation of Rice’s Theorem concerning equivalence classes of programs and show how it can be used to study intensional properties such as time and space complexity. While many results that follow from our general theorems can - and have - been proved by more involved, specialised methods, our results are sufficiently simple that little work is needed to apply them.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Moyen, Jean Yves","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-476330"],"event":{"acronym":"CIE","end":"2019-07-19","place":"Durham, gb","start":"2019-07-15","title":"15th Conference on Computability in Europe, CiE 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"more intensional versions of rice s theorem","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85069513483&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-476330","identifier":[{"id":"85069513483","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8aa823e2-70c8-4ba6-b13a-f9a42e999362"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5AC1907DB544B10521D33AC6996C4D44"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Programming Languages and Theory of Computation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jean Yves","key":"moyenpau","last":"Moyen","name":"Moyen, Jean Yves","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Barnaby","key":"martinpedh","last":"Martin","name":"Martin, Barnaby","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniël","key":"paulusmapedh","last":"Paulusma","name":"Paulusma, Daniël","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Giuseppe","key":"primieropedh","last":"Primiero","name":"Primiero, Giuseppe","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Florin","key":"maneapedh","last":"Manea","name":"Manea, Florin","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-22996-2_19","isbn":["9783030229955"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"217-229","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Computing with Foresight and Industry - 15th Conference on Computability in Europe, CiE 2019, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85069513483"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8aa823e2-70c8-4ba6-b13a-f9a42e999362"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"More Intensional Versions of Rice’s Theorem","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-476330","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We contribute the largest publicly available dataset of naturally occurring factual claims for the purpose of automatic claim verification. It is collected from 26 fact checking websites in English, paired with textual sources and rich metadata, and labelled for veracity by human expert journalists. We present an in-depth analysis of the dataset, highlighting characteristics and challenges. Further, we present results for automatic veracity prediction, both with established baselines and with a novel method for joint ranking of evidence pages and predicting veracity that outperforms all baselines. Significant performance increases are achieved by encoding evidence, and by modelling metadata. Our best-performing model achieves a Macro F1 of 49.2%, showing that this is a challenging testbed for claim veracity prediction.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Augenstein, Isabelle","Lioma, Christina","Wang, Dongsheng","Chaves Lima, Lucas","Hansen, Casper","Hansen, Christian","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-396134"],"event":{"acronym":"EMNLP","end":"2019-11-07","place":"Hong Kong, cn","start":"2019-11-03","title":"2019 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing and the 9th International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing (EMNLP-IJCNLP)","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multifc a real world multi domain dataset for evidence based fact checking of claims","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/D19-1475","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-396134","identifier":[{"id":"85084294351","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0472b943-e7d8-4bee-802a-e916a3389b26"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-E5E80D55E8B6E21C1DE7060F8E3AC4B5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/239563734/OA_MultiFC.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/D19-1475","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Isabelle","key":"augensteinisabellepau","last":"Augenstein","locid":"929ec255-2eae-4e6d-b826-5e7abd210f06","name":"Augenstein, Isabelle","orcid":"0000-0003-1562-7909","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"liomachristinapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dongsheng","key":"wangdongshengpau","last":"Wang","locid":"f2733e51-5609-4c76-aefa-d1b9b1e8776b","name":"Wang, Dongsheng","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lucas","key":"chaveslimalucaspau","last":"Chaves Lima","locid":"be768ab9-a6c8-4b2e-a678-eb5efc4c339f","name":"Chaves Lima, Lucas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Casper","key":"hansencasperpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"0f5313ce-6e55-41ec-88c7-8368f583f459","name":"Hansen, Casper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hansenchristianpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"58729b14-2de9-4102-91e9-8d2bc16b539e","name":"Hansen, Christian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenjakobgruepau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/d19-1475","pages":"4684-4697","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2019 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing and the 9th International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing (EMNLP-IJCNLP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084294351"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0472b943-e7d8-4bee-802a-e916a3389b26"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"MultiFC : A Real-World Multi-Domain Dataset for Evidence-Based Fact Checking of Claims","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-396134","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Recurrent neural networks (RNNs) can model natural language by sequentially”reading” input tokens and outputting a distributed representation of each token. Due to the sequential nature of RNNs, inference time is linearly dependent on the input length, and all inputs are read regardless of their importance. Efforts to speed up this inference, known as”neural speed reading”, either ignore or skim over part of the input. We present Structural-Jump-LSTM: the first neural speed reading model to both skip and jump text during inference. The model consists of a standard LSTM and two agents: one capable of skipping single words when reading, and one capable of exploiting punctuation structure (sub-sentence separators (,:), sentence end symbols (.!?), or end of text markers) to jump ahead after reading a word. A comprehensive experimental evaluation of our model against all five state-of-the-art neural reading models shows that Structural-Jump-LSTM achieves the best overall floating point operations (FLOP) reduction (hence is faster), while keeping the same accuracy or even improving it compared to a vanilla LSTM that reads the whole text.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hansen, Christian","Hansen, Casper","Alstrup, Stephen","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Lioma, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-441679"],"event":{"end":"2019-05-09","place":"New Orleans, us","start":"2019-05-06","title":"7th International Conference on Learning Representations, ICLR 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neural speed reading with structural jump lstm","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-441679","ids":["ku-50c90ae9-9338-49a9-bda6-1f244b3bc978"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-107970C9D78247AD2ED991662D2B5775"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hansenchristianpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"58729b14-2de9-4102-91e9-8d2bc16b539e","name":"Hansen, Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Casper","key":"hansencasperpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"0f5313ce-6e55-41ec-88c7-8368f583f459","name":"Hansen, Casper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stephen","key":"alstrupstephenpau","last":"Alstrup","locid":"6d1b63fb-235a-4932-8345-413b4ac8d6a5","name":"Alstrup, Stephen","orcid":"0000-0001-7896-8386","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenjakobgruepau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"liomachristinapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-50c90ae9-9338-49a9-bda6-1f244b3bc978"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Neural speed reading with structural-jump-LSTM","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-441679","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This paper describes the winning approach used by the Copenhagen team in the CLEF-2019 CheckThat! lab. Given a political debate or speech, the aim is to predict which sentences should be prioritized for fact-checking by creating a ranked list of sentences. While many approaches for check-worthiness exist, we are the first to directly optimize the sentence ranking as all previous work has solely used standard classification based loss functions. We present a recurrent neural network model that learns a sentence encoding, from which a check-worthiness score is predicted. The model is trained by jointly optimizing a binary cross entropy loss, as well as a ranking based pairwise hinge loss. We obtain sentence pairs for training through contrastive sampling, where for each sentence we find the k most semantically similar sentences with opposite label. To increase the generalizability of the model, we utilize weak supervision by using an existing check-worthiness approach to weakly label a large unlabeled dataset. We experimentally show that both weak supervision and the ranking component improve the results individually (MAP increases of 25% and 9% respectively), while when used together improve the results even more (39% increase). Through a comparison to existing state-of-the-art check-worthiness methods, we find that our approach improves the MAP score by 11%.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hansen, Casper","Hansen, Christian","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Lioma, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-453191"],"event":{"acronym":"CLEF","end":"2019-09-12","place":"Lugano, ch","start":"2019-09-09","title":"20th Working Notes of CLEF Conference and Labs of the Evaluation Forum, CLEF 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Contrastive ranking","Neural networks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neural weakly supervised fact check worthiness detection with contrastive sampling based ranking loss","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/253233206/paper_56.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-453191","identifier":[{"id":"85070534030","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-63ee4db9-bd93-4ad1-85fd-980aeda1a883"],"keyword":["Contrastive ranking","Fact check-worthiness","Neural networks"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-59EA00F1D9A40A847D2EED051CA53AB3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/253233206/paper_56.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2380/paper_56.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Casper","key":"hansencasperpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"0f5313ce-6e55-41ec-88c7-8368f583f459","name":"Hansen, Casper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hansenchristianpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"58729b14-2de9-4102-91e9-8d2bc16b539e","name":"Hansen, Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenjakobgruepau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"liomachristinapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16130073"],"journal":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","status":"p","title":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","volume":"2380"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85070534030"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-63ee4db9-bd93-4ad1-85fd-980aeda1a883"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Neural weakly supervised fact check-worthiness detection with contrastive sampling-based ranking loss","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-453191","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Automatic fact-checking systems detect misinformation, such as fake news, by (i) selecting check-worthy sentences for fact-checking, (ii) gathering related information to the sentences, and (iii) inferring the factuality of the sentences. Most prior research on (i) uses hand-crafted features to select check-worthy sentences, and does not explicitly account for the recent finding that the top weighted terms in both check-worthy and non-check-worthy sentences are actually overlapping [15]. Motivated by this, we present a neural check-worthiness sentence ranking model that represents each word in a sentence by both its embedding (aiming to capture its semantics) and its syntactic dependencies (aiming to capture its role in modifying the semantics of other terms in the sentence). Our model is an end-to-end trainable neural network for check-worthiness ranking, which is trained on large amounts of unlabelled data through weak supervision. Thorough experimental evaluation against state of the art baselines, with and without weak supervision, shows our model to be superior at all times (+13% in MAP and +28% at various Precision cut-offs from the best baseline with statistical significance). Empirical analysis of the use of weak supervision, word embedding pretraining on domain-specific data, and the use of syntactic dependencies of our model reveals that check-worthy sentences contain notably more identical syntactic dependencies than non-check-worthy sentences.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hansen, Casper","Hansen, Christian","Alstrup, Stephen","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Lioma, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-462448"],"event":{"acronym":"thewebconf","end":"2019-05-17","place":"San Francisco, us","start":"2019-05-13","title":"2019 World Wide Web Conference, WWW 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Check worthiness","Deep learning","Fact checking","Weak supervision"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neural check worthiness ranking with weak supervision finding sentences for fact checking","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3308560.3316736","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-462448","identifier":[{"id":"85066888862","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7368d612-cc67-46b4-ad58-253196776cb2"],"keyword":["Check worthiness","Deep learning","Fact checking","Weak supervision"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C9247217A2862262D2EFCB5666F24940"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/223251765/p994_hansen.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3308560.3316736","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Casper","key":"hansencasperpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"0f5313ce-6e55-41ec-88c7-8368f583f459","name":"Hansen, Casper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hansenchristianpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"58729b14-2de9-4102-91e9-8d2bc16b539e","name":"Hansen, Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stephen","key":"alstrupstephenpau","last":"Alstrup","locid":"6d1b63fb-235a-4932-8345-413b4ac8d6a5","name":"Alstrup, Stephen","orcid":"0000-0001-7896-8386","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenjakobgruepau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"liomachristinapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3308560.3316736","eisbn":["9781450366755"],"pages":"994-1000","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"The Web Conference 2019 - Companion of the World Wide Web Conference, WWW 2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066888862"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7368d612-cc67-46b4-ad58-253196776cb2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Neural check-worthiness ranking with weak supervision : Finding sentences for fact-checking","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-462448","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"When the meaning of a phrase cannot be inferred from the individual meanings of its words (e.g., hot dog), that phrase is said to be non-compositional. Automatic compositionality detection in multiword phrases is critical in any application of semantic processing, such as search engines [9]; failing to detect non-compositional phrases can hurt system effectiveness notably. Existing research treats phrases as either compositional or non-compositional in a deterministic manner. In this paper, we operationalize the viewpoint that compositionality is contextual rather than deterministic, i.e., that whether a phrase is compositional or non-compositional depends on its context. For example, the phrase �green card� is compositional when referring to a green colored card, whereas it is non-compositional when meaning permanent residence authorization. We address the challenge of detecting this type of contextual compositionality as follows: given a multi-word phrase, we enrich the word embedding representing its semantics with evidence about its global context (terms it often collocates with) as well as its local context (narratives where that phrase is used, which we call usage scenarios). We further extend this representation with information extracted from external knowledge bases. The resulting representation incorporates both localized context and more general usage of the phrase and allows to detect its compositionality in a non-deterministic and contextual way. Empirical evaluation of our model on a dataset of phrase compositionality1, manually collected by crowdsourcing contextual compositionality assessments, shows that our model outperforms state-of-the-art baselines notably on detecting phrase compositionality.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wang, Dongsheng","Li, Qiuchi","Chaves Lima, Lucas","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Lioma, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-471287"],"event":{"acronym":"thewebconf","end":"2019-05-17","place":"San Francisco, us","start":"2019-05-13","title":"2019 World Wide Web Conference, WWW 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Padua"],"keyword":["Compositionality detection","Knowledge base","Word embedding"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"contextual compositionality detection with external knowledge bases and word embeddings","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3308560.3316584","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-471287","identifier":[{"id":"85066890169","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-821dffe2-2486-4489-8b0b-3adae4c297e0"],"keyword":["Compositionality detection","Knowledge base","Word embedding"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7CEEF664AA1D94CDE733A83F6E017894"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3308560.3316584","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/223251964/p317_wang.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of padua","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Padua","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Dongsheng","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"f2733e51-5609-4c76-aefa-d1b9b1e8776b","name":"Wang, Dongsheng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Qiuchi","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Qiuchi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lucas Chaves","key":"limapau","last":"Lima","locid":"be768ab9-a6c8-4b2e-a678-eb5efc4c339f","name":"Chaves Lima, Lucas","name_org":"Lima, Lucas Chaves","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"liomapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3308560.3316584","eisbn":["9781450366755"],"pages":"317-323","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"The Web Conference 2019 - Companion of the World Wide Web Conference, WWW 2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066890169"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-821dffe2-2486-4489-8b0b-3adae4c297e0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Contextual compositionality detection with external knowledge bases and word embeddings","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-471287","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We predict which claim in a political debate should be prioritized for fact-checking. A particular challenge is, given a debate, how to produce a ranked list of its sentences based on their worthiness for fact checking. We develop a Recurrent Neural Network (RNN) model that learns a sentence embedding, which is then used to predict the checkworthiness of a sentence. Our sentence embedding encodes both semantic and syntactic dependencies using pretrained word2vec word embeddings as well as part-of-speech tagging and syntactic dependency parsing. This results in a multi-representation of each word, which we use as input to a RNN with GRU memory units; the output from each word is aggregated using attention, followed by a fully connected layer, from which the output is predicted using a sigmoid function. The overall performance of our techniques is successful, achieving the overall second best performing run (MAP: 0.1152) in the competition, as well as the highest overall performance (MAP: 0.1810) for our contrastive run with a 32% improvement over the second highest MAP score in the English language category. In our primary run we combined our sentence embedding with state of the art check-worthy features, whereas in the contrastive run we considered our sentence embedding alone","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hansen, Casper","Hansen, Christian","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Lioma, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-397418"],"event":{"acronym":"CLEF","end":"2018-09-14","place":"Avignon, fr","start":"2018-09-10","title":"19th Working Notes of CLEF Conference and Labs of the Evaluation Forum, CLEF 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CNN","Fact checking","Political debates","RNN"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the copenhagen team participation in the check worthiness task of the competition of automatic identification and verification of claims in political debates of the clef 000000002018 checkthat lab","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/202539750/paper_81.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-397418","ids":["ku-069c4426-de2a-431d-ba28-d3f3eaab606c"],"keyword":["CNN","Fact checking","Political debates","RNN"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-DB893B79FF363D5A095B7A0C516A48BB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/202539750/paper_81.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Programming Languages (APL)","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Casper","key":"hansencasperpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"0f5313ce-6e55-41ec-88c7-8368f583f459","name":"Hansen, Casper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hansenchristianpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"58729b14-2de9-4102-91e9-8d2bc16b539e","name":"Hansen, Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenjakobgruepau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"liomachristinapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Linda","key":"cappellatolindapedh","last":"Cappellato","name":"Cappellato, Linda","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Nicola","key":"ferronicolapedh","last":"Ferro","name":"Ferro, Nicola","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jian-Yun","key":"niejianyunpedh","last":"Nie","name":"Nie, Jian-Yun","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Laure","key":"soulierlaurepedh","last":"Soulier","name":"Soulier, Laure","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"10","issn":["16130073"],"publisher":"CEUR-WS.org","series":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","status":"p","title":"CLEF 2018 Working Notes"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85051073733"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-069c4426-de2a-431d-ba28-d3f3eaab606c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Copenhagen Team Participation in the Check-Worthiness Task of the Competition of Automatic Identification and Verification of Claims in Political Debates of the CLEF-2018 CheckThat! Lab","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-397418","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Recent results indicate that static graph features might not be adequate to solve challenges in graphs involving a temporal dimension. We analyze several classification problems using already established temporal metrics, and we propose label-sensitive and recency-sensitive variants of these metrics that capture labeling information and additional temporal patterns in the data. We test all new and old metrics, and a baseline based on a standard disease-spreading model, using tuned off-the-shelf classifiers on 9 datasets of varying size and usage domain. Our experiments indicate that usage of label-and recency-sensitive metrics on real-world data provides more accurate results than static approaches and approaches based on temporal metrics alone.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ryther, Christopher","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-478854"],"event":{"acronym":"ICDM","end":"2018-11-20","place":"Singapore, Singapore","start":"2018-11-17","title":"2018 IEEE International Conference on Data Mining Workshops (ICDMW)","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"within network classification in temporal graphs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/8637363/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-478854","identifier":[{"id":"85062858878","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8edfda51-7516-4765-b2ff-db9402374397"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FCDCC1C9517F0D5BDCA7D04A43A172EB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christopher","key":"rytherpau","last":"Ryther","locid":"ed0078c4-9ccf-47c2-8d38-a471414fbee1","name":"Ryther, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0001-9060-2707","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","name_org":"Simonsen, Jakob","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icdmw.2018.00041","pages":"229-236","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings, 2018 IEEE International Conference on Data Mining Workshops (ICDMW)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85062858878"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8edfda51-7516-4765-b2ff-db9402374397"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Within-Network Classification in Temporal Graphs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-478854","year":"2018","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We consider the partition lattice $\\Pi_\\kappa$ on any set of transfinite cardinality $\\kappa$, and properties of $\\Pi_\\kappa$ whose analogues do not hold for finite cardinalities. Assuming the Axiom of Choice we prove: (I) the cardinality of any maximal well-ordered chain is between the cofinality $\\mathrm{cf}(\\kappa)$ and $\\kappa$, and $\\kappa$ always occurs as the cardinality of a maximal well-ordered chain; (II) there are maximal chains in $\\Pi_\\kappa$ of cardinality $> \\kappa$; (III) if, for every ordinal $\\delta$ with $|\\delta| $ 2$.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Avery, James Emil","Moyen, Jean-Yves","Ruzicka, Pavel","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-444073"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Czechia","France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Charles University","Université Sorbonne Paris Nord"],"keyword":["math RA"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chains antichains and complements in infinite partition lattices","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/license.html","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.05284","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-444073","identifier":[{"id":"85045969891","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-54be2faf-e45c-45d4-9938-dd1b575e502b"],"keyword":["06B05 (Primary), 06C15 (Secondary)","math.RA"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0463A37302F1AA1FD3333EA9DDDF20A6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/license.html","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.05284","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Xray and Neutron Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, eScience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"université sorbonne paris nord","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université Sorbonne Paris Nord","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cz","key":"charles university","loc":["Czechia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Charles University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"James Emil","key":"averypau","last":"Avery","locid":"41079901-31dc-4e1b-9e75-86ad49e73136","name":"Avery, James Emil","orcid":"0000-0001-7772-3440","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jean-Yves","key":"moyenpau","last":"Moyen","name":"Moyen, Jean-Yves","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Pavel","key":"ruzickapau","last":"Ruzicka","name":"Ruzicka, Pavel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00012-018-0514-z","issn":["00025240","14208911"],"issn_org":["00025240"],"issue":"37","journal":"Algebra Universalis","paperid":"37","status":"p","title":"Algebra Universalis","volume":"79"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85045969891"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-54be2faf-e45c-45d4-9938-dd1b575e502b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Chains, antichains, and complements in infinite partition lattices","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-444073","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Given a set of political debate claims that have been already identified as worth checking, we consider the task of automatically checking the factuality of these claims. In particular, given a sentence that is worth checking, the goal is for the system to determine whether the claim is likely to be true, false, half-true or that it is unsure of its factuality. We implement a variety of models, including Bayes, SVM, RNN, to either step-wise assist our model or work as potential baselines. Then, we develop additional multi-scale Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) with different kernel sizes that learn from external sources whether a claim is true, false, half-true or unsure as follows: we treat claims as search engine queries and step-wise retrieve the top-N documents from Google with as much original claim as possible. We strategically select most relevant but sufficient documents with respect to the claims, and extract features, such as title, total number of results returned, and snippet to train the prediction model. We submitted results of SVM and CNNs, and the overall performance of our techniques is successful, achieving the overall best performing run (with lowest error rate 0.7050 from our SVM and highest accuracy 46.76% from our CNNs) in the competition.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Wang, Dongsheng","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Larsen, Birger","Lioma, Christina"],"cuid":["S02-091.67-011482"],"event":{"acronym":"CLEF","end":"2018-09-14","place":"Avignon, fr","start":"2018-09-10","title":"19th Working Notes of CLEF Conference and Labs of the Evaluation Forum, CLEF 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["CNN","Fact checking","Political debates","RNN"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":[