{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Kop, Cynthia Louisa Martina","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-434845"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"complexity hierarchies and higher order cons free term rewriting","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.23638/LMCS-13(3:8)2017","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-434845","identifier":[{"id":"000419163000020","type":"wos"},{"id":"85041852341","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-455ebc9b-6981-476b-8663-0b82ad7b294a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-7846FA8F26D61102D76B2DBA4F5FEBF0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/189255279/Kop_2017_Complexity_hierarchies.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.23638/LMCS-13(3:8)2017","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Cynthia Louisa Martina","key":"koppau","last":"Kop","locid":"a2bb0a9d-00af-4ecf-b763-e9af8539c68a","name":"Kop, Cynthia Louisa Martina","orcid":"0000-0002-6337-2544","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.23638/lmcs-13(3:8)2017","issn":["18605974"],"issue":"3","journal":"Logical Methods in Computer Science","paperid":"8","status":"p","title":"Logical Methods in Computer Science","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85041852341"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-455ebc9b-6981-476b-8663-0b82ad7b294a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Complexity hierarchies and higher-order cons-free term rewriting","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-434845","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The paper studies continuous-time Markov chains (CTMCs) as transformers of real-valued functions on their state space, considered as generalised predicates and called observables. Markov chains are assumed to take values in a countable state space S; observables f: S → ℝ may be unbounded. The interpretation of CTMCs as transformers of observables is via their transition function Pt: each observable f is mapped to the observable Ptf that, in turn, maps each state x to the mean value of f at time t conditioned on being in state x at time 0. The first result is computability of the time evolution of observables, i.e., maps of the form (t, f) ↦ Ptf, under conditions that imply existence of a Banach sequence space of observables on which the transition function Pt of a fixed CTMC induces a family of bounded linear operators that vary continuously in time (w.r.t. the usual topology on bounded operators). The second result is PTIME-computability of the projections t ↦ (Ptf)(x), for each state x, provided that the rate matrix of the CTMC Xt is locally algebraic on a subspace containing the observable f. The results are flexible enough to accommodate unbounded observables; explicit examples feature the token counts in stochastic Petri nets and sub-string occurrences of stochastic string rewriting systems. The results provide a functional analytic alternative to Monte Carlo simulation as test bed for mean-field approximations, moment closure, and similar techniques that are fast, but lack absolute error guarantees.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Danos, Vincent","Heindel, Tobias","Garnier, Ilias","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-539221"],"event":{"acronym":"FoSSaCS","end":"2017-04-29","place":"Uppsala, se","start":"2017-04-22","title":"20th International Conference on Foundations of Software Science and Computation Structures","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["France","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Edinburgh","École Normale Supérieure"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"computing continuous time markov chains as transformers of unbounded observables","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85015940232&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-539221","identifier":[{"id":"85015940232","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f43ad1b6-a003-42e0-b4e9-feae1f55ad2a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4C127FDC44DA33AC49C7F448BF37722E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fr","key":"école normale supérieure","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"École Normale Supérieure","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Edinburgh","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Vincent","key":"danospau","last":"Danos","name":"Danos, Vincent","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Tobias","key":"heindelpau","last":"Heindel","locid":"6b0bc87f-e204-4d0b-a0e4-c3549708a3b9","name":"Heindel, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0003-3371-8564","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Ilias","key":"garnierpau","last":"Garnier","name":"Garnier, Ilias","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Javier","key":"esparzapedh","last":"Esparza","name":"Esparza, Javier","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrzej S.","key":"murawskipedh","last":"Murawski","name":"Murawski, Andrzej S.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-54458-7_20","eisbn":["9783662544587"],"isbn":["9783662544570"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"338-354","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture notes in computer science","status":"p","subtitle":"20th International Conference, FOSSACS 2017, Held as Part of the European Joint Conferences on Theory and Practice of Software, ETAPS 2017, Uppsala, Sweden, April 22-29, 2017, Proceedings","title":"Foundations of Software Science and Computation Structures"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85015940232"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f43ad1b6-a003-42e0-b4e9-feae1f55ad2a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Computing continuous-time Markov chains as transformers of unbounded observables","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-539221","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"User experience, commonly abbreviated UX, is a ubiquitous term in human-computer interaction, yet the term carries different semantics and connotations to practitioners across the field. While the exact definition of the term has been hotly debated in academic circles, the modern view appears to be largely divided into two, complementary, approaches: One that recognizes that User Experience is a collection of theory, methodology and practice from a number of disparate scientific disciplines, all with the same overarching aim of studying the experiential aspects of human interaction with technological artifacts; and another that uses such theory, methodology and practice integrated in the design of such technological artifacts, typically under the slogan User Experience design. While the academic debate of an exact definition of, and foundation for the principles of, User Experience still generates discussion, this chapter aims at giving an overview of extant views of User Experience with particular attention to the multi-faceted and multi-disciplinary nature of the subject as used by researchers and practitioners in the field.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-462770"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Usability","User Experience Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"user experience","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85049704502&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-462770","identifier":[{"id":"85049704502","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-73eedbaf-4710-4f4c-8797-4b968bc3052a"],"keyword":["Usability","User Experience Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C1AD2A38CEE2CD585D19F3C77F7351F7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Programming Languages and Theory of Computation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/9781118976005.ch10","eisbn":["9781118976005"],"isbn":["9781118976135"],"pages":"191-206","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"The Wiley Handbook of Human Computer Interaction Set","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85049704502"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-73eedbaf-4710-4f4c-8797-4b968bc3052a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"User Experience","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-462770","year":"2017","yearsub":"2019"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Moyen, Jean-Yves","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-509924"],"event":{"end":"2017-04-23","place":"Uppsala, se","start":"2017-04-22","title":"8th Workshop on Developments in Implicit Computational Complexity and 5th Workshop on Foundational and Practical Aspects of Resource Analysis","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"computability in the lattice of equivalence relations","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.248.8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-509924","identifier":[{"id":"85030157660","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-c32336a4-b937-45f4-bd04-f8d55c4a8bdd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-65911CAD36CD88A58995D1125F338F00"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.248.8","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/178883780/Moyen_2017_Computability_in_the_lattice.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jean-Yves","key":"moyenpau","last":"Moyen","locid":"a9591ca0-6928-4376-92ef-0b2881460792","name":"Moyen, Jean-Yves","orcid":"0000-0002-6883-6993","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Guillaume","key":"bonfantepedh","last":"Bonfante","name":"Bonfante, Guillaume","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Georg","key":"moserpedh","last":"Moser","name":"Moser, Georg","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4204/eptcs.248.8","issn":["20752180"],"pages":"38-46","publisher":"Open Publishing Association","series":"Electronic Proceedings in Theoretical Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Proceedings 8th Workshop on Developments in Implicit Computational Complexity and 5th Workshop on Foundational and Practical Aspects of Resource Analysis"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85030157660"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c32336a4-b937-45f4-bd04-f8d55c4a8bdd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Computability in the lattice of equivalence relations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-509924","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Recent discussions on alternative facts, fake news, and post truth politics have motivated research on creating technologies that allow people not only to access information, but also to assess the credibility of the information presented to them by information retrieval systems. Whereas technology is in place for filtering information according to relevance and/or credibility [15], no single measure currently exists for evaluating the accuracy or precision (and more generally effectiveness) of both the relevance and the credibility of retrieved results. One obvious way of doing so is to measure relevance and credibility effectiveness separately, and then consolidate the two measures into one. There at least two problems with such an approach: (I) it is not certain that the same criteria are applied to the evaluation of both relevance and credibility (and applying different criteria introduces bias to the evaluation); (II) many more and richer measures exist for assessing relevance effectiveness than for assessing credibility effectiveness (hence risking further bias). Motivated by the above, we present two novel types of evaluation measures that are designed to measure the effectiveness of both relevance and credibility in ranked lists of retrieval results. Experimental evaluation on a small human-annotated dataset (that we make freely available to the research community) shows that our measures are expressive and intuitive in their interpretation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Lioma, Christina","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Larsen, Birger"],"cuid":["S02-095.68-003346"],"event":{"acronym":"ICTIR","end":"2017-10-04","place":"Amsterdam, nl","start":"2017-10-01","title":"7th ACM SIGIR International Conference on the Theory of Information Retrieval, ICTIR 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Credibility","Evaluation measures","Relevance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation measures for relevance and credibility in ranked lists","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85033232681&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.68-003346","identifier":[{"id":"85033232681","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-4433bba6-ec20-4e28-a570-5e5d6fe4b9ab","ku-cfa2bfe1-fbc4-4e15-bd7f-6e1e5efb004b"],"keyword":["Credibility","Evaluation measures","Relevance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DE6496CE6022014AC6DAD4C67C1214AA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The Image Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Responsible Impact","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"liomapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birger","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9cb12135-a825-43ba-87e2-b71651b91939","name":"Larsen, Birger","orcid":"0000-0002-3622-2698","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3121050.3121072","eisbn":["9781450344906"],"pages":"91-98","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"ICTIR 2017 - Proceedings of the 2017 ACM SIGIR International Conference on the Theory of Information Retrieval"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85033232681"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4433bba6-ec20-4e28-a570-5e5d6fe4b9ab","ku-cfa2bfe1-fbc4-4e15-bd7f-6e1e5efb004b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evaluation measures for relevance and credibility in ranked lists","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.68-003346","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We investigate the power of non-determinism in purely functional programming languages with higher-order types. Specifically, we consider cons-free programs of varying data orders, equipped with explicit non-deterministic choice. Cons-freeness roughly means that data constructors cannot occur in function bodies and all manipulation of storage space thus has to happen indirectly using the call stack. While cons-free programs have previously been used by several authors to characterise complexity classes, the work on non-deterministic programs has almost exclusively considered programs of data order 0. Previous work has shown that adding explicit non-determinism to consfree programs taking data of order 0 does not increase expressivity; we prove that this—dramatically—is not the case for higher data orders: adding non-determinism to programs with data order at least 1 allows for a characterisation of the entire class of elementary-time decidable sets. Finally we show how, even with non-deterministic choice, the original hierarchy of characterisations is restored by imposing different restrictions.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kop, Cynthia Louisa Martina","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-400127"],"event":{"acronym":"ESOP","end":"2017-04-29","place":"Uppsala, se","start":"2017-04-22","title":"26th European Symposium on Programming","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the power of non determinism in higher order implicit complexity characterising complexity classes using non deterministic cons free programming","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/pdf/1701.05382","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-400127","identifier":[{"id":"85018691937","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0b2710fa-a933-43a3-a06c-1c740b56e5a6"],"keyword":["Cons-free programming","EXPTIME hierarchy","Implicit computational complexity","Non-deterministic programming","Unitary variables"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-868ECF1A05137E365968741D239A0718"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/pdf/1701.05382","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Cynthia Louisa Martina","key":"koppau","last":"Kop","locid":"a2bb0a9d-00af-4ecf-b763-e9af8539c68a","name":"Kop, Cynthia Louisa Martina","orcid":"0000-0002-6337-2544","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hongseok","key":"yangpedh","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Hongseok","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-54434-1_25","eisbn":["9783662544341"],"isbn":["9783662544334"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"668-695","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture notes in computer science","status":"p","subtitle":"26th European Symposium on Programming, ESOP 2017, Held as Part of the European Joint Conferences on Theory and Practice of Software, ETAPS 2017, Uppsala, Sweden, April 22–29, 2017, Proceedings","title":"Programming Languages and Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85018691937"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0b2710fa-a933-43a3-a06c-1c740b56e5a6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The power of non-determinism in higher-order implicit complexity : characterising complexity classes using non-deterministic cons-free programming","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-400127","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Kop, Cynthia Louisa Martina","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-479926"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-26","place":"Porto, pt","start":"2016-06-22","title":"International Conference on Formal Structures for Computation and Deduction 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"complexity hierarchies and higher order cons free rewriting","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2016.23","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-479926","identifier":[{"id":"84977518642","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-90bd8750-5ab8-442c-9222-014d6a7bb65c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-2855645131B514A92FA53BF8452BC9A7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2016.23","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/169109517/Kop_2016_Complexity_hierarchies.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Cynthia Louisa Martina","key":"koppau","last":"Kop","locid":"a2bb0a9d-00af-4ecf-b763-e9af8539c68a","name":"Kop, Cynthia Louisa Martina","orcid":"0000-0002-6337-2544","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Delia","key":"kesnerpedh","last":"Kesner","name":"Kesner, Delia","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Brigitte","key":"pientkapedh","last":"Pientka","name":"Pientka, Brigitte","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.fscd.2016.23","isbn":["9783959770101"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","status":"p","title":"1st International Conference on Formal Structures for Computation and Deduction (FSCD 2016)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84977518642"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-90bd8750-5ab8-442c-9222-014d6a7bb65c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Complexity hierarchies and higher-order cons-free rewriting","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-479926","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The spectrum of a first-order sentence is the set of natural numbers occurring as the cardinalities of finite models of the sentence. In a recent survey, Durand et al. introduce a new class of real numbers, the spectral reals, induced by spectra and pose two open problems associated to this class. In the present note, we answer these open problems as well as other open problems from an earlier, unpublished version of the survey. Specifically, we prove that (i) every algebraic real is spectral, (ii) every automatic real is spectral, (iii) the subword density of a spectral real is either 0 or 1, and both may occur, and (iv) every right-computable real number between 0 and 1 occurs as the subword entropy of a spectral real. In addition, Durand et al. note that the set of spectral reals is not closed under addition or multiplication. We extend this result by showing that the class of spectral reals is not closed under any computable operation satisfying some mild conditions.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jakobsen, Sune","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-455236"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computational complexity","First order logic"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"some remarks on real numbers induced by first order spectra","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-455236","identifier":[{"id":"84978818229","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-677e400d-b0ec-44c7-92cd-1611626879ac"],"keyword":["Computability theory","Computational complexity","First-order logic","Spectral reals"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-5CBDA755F95C622F95115C68A01DE724"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sune","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"11725a0f-5fba-4671-ab9e-4e4647a2b7e0","name":"Jakobsen, Sune","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1215/00294527-3489987","issn":["00294527","19390726"],"issn_org":["00294527"],"issue":"3","journal":"Notre Dame Journal of Formal Logic","pages":"355-368","status":"p","title":"Notre Dame Journal of Formal Logic","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84978818229"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-677e400d-b0ec-44c7-92cd-1611626879ac"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Some remarks on real numbers induced by first-order spectra","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-455236","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Divergence From Randomness (DFR) ranking models assume that informative terms are distributed in a corpus differently than non-informative terms. Different statistical models (e.g. Poisson, geometric) are used to model the distribution of non-informative terms, producing different DFR models. An informative term is then detected by measuring the divergence of its distribution from the distribution of non-informative terms. However, there is little empirical evidence that the distributions of non-informative terms used in DFR actually fit current datasets. Practically this risks providing a poor separation between informative and non-informative terms, thus compromising the discriminative power of the ranking model. We present a novel extension to DFR, which first detects the best-fitting distribution of non-informative terms in a collection, and then adapts the ranking computation to this best-fitting distribution. We call this model Adaptive Distributional Ranking (ADR) because it adapts the ranking to the statistics of the specific dataset being processed each time. Experiments on TREC data show ADR to outperform DFR models (and their extensions) and be comparable in performance to a query likelihood language model (LM).","author_count":4,"contributors":["Petersen, Casper","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Järvelin, Kalervo","Lioma, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-470086"],"event":{"acronym":"CIKM","end":"2016-10-28","place":"Indianapolis, us","start":"2016-10-24","title":"25th ACM International Conference on Information and Knowledge Management","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["cs IR"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adaptive distributional extensions to dfr ranking","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-470086","identifier":[{"id":"84996602497","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-80093e83-6908-4ef3-b0db-97d01d0c317f"],"keyword":["cs.IR"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4FE0FF5D655BB2939F601758EE651DDB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The Image Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Casper","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"b3f33831-f74d-423e-ab97-6e864f3ecc89","name":"Petersen, Casper","orcid":"0000-0001-5858-1985","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kalervo","key":"järvelinpau","last":"Järvelin","name":"Järvelin, Kalervo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"liomapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2983323.2983895","eisbn":["9781450340731"],"pages":"2005-2008","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 25th ACM International Conference on Information and Knowledge Management"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84996602497"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-80093e83-6908-4ef3-b0db-97d01d0c317f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Adaptive distributional extensions to DFR ranking","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-470086","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"What if Information Retrieval (IR) systems did not just retrieve relevant information that is stored in their indices, but could also \"understand\" it and synthesise it into a single document? We present a preliminary study that makes a first step towards answering this question. Given a query, we train a Recurrent Neural Network (RNN) on existing relevant information to that query. We then use the RNN to \"deep learn\" a single, synthetic, and we assume, relevant document for that query. We design a crowdsourcing experiment to assess how relevant the \"deep learned\" document is, compared to existing relevant documents. Users are shown a query and four wordclouds (of three existing relevant documents and our deep learned synthetic document). The synthetic document is ranked on average most relevant of all.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lioma, Christina","Larsen, Birger","Petersen, Casper","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S02-088.31-003821"],"event":{"end":"2016-07-21","place":"Pisa, it","start":"2016-07-21","title":"Neu-IR '16 SIGIR Workshop on Neural Information Retrieval, July 21, 2016, Pisa, Italy","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["The Image Section"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deep learning relevance creating relevant information as opposed to retrieving it","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.07660","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-088.31-003821","ids":["aau-4e5697dc-ac3e-4255-8c93-4afe42773b79","ku-9514a731-c0b8-449c-8c4e-347b43cb1643"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-5D6667F442A28485C62B10B88DD62510"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.07660","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The Image Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["The Image Section"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Datalogisk Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Responsible Impact","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Christina","key":"liomapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birger","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9cb12135-a825-43ba-87e2-b71651b91939","name":"Larsen, Birger","orcid":"0000-0002-3622-2698","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Casper","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"b3f33831-f74d-423e-ab97-6e864f3ecc89","name":"Petersen, Casper","orcid":"0000-0001-5858-1985","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Neu-IR '16 SIGIR Workshop on Neural Information Retrieval, July 21, 2016, Pisa, Italy"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4e5697dc-ac3e-4255-8c93-4afe42773b79","ku-9514a731-c0b8-449c-8c4e-347b43cb1643"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Deep Learning Relevance : Creating Relevant Information (as Opposed to Retrieving it)","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.31-003821","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Document coherence describes how much sense text makes in terms of its logical organisation and discourse flow. Even though coherence is a relatively difficult notion to quantify precisely, it can be approximated automatically. This type of coherence modelling is not only interesting in itself, but also useful for a number of other text processing tasks, including Information Retrieval (IR), where adjusting the ranking of documents according to both their relevance and their coherence has been shown to increase retrieval effectiveness [34, 37]. The state of the art in unsupervised coherence modelling represents documents as bipartite graphs of sentences and discourse entities, and then projects these bipartite graphs into one-mode undirected graphs. However, one-mode projections may incur significant loss of the information present in the original bipartite structure. To address this we present three novel graph metrics that compute document coherence on the original bipartite graph of sentences and entities. Evaluation on standard settings shows that: (i) one of our coherence metrics beats the state of the art in terms of coherence accuracy; and (ii) all three of our coherence metrics improve retrieval effectiveness because, as closer analysis reveals, they capture aspects of document quality that go undetected by both keyword-based standard ranking and by spam filtering. This work contributes document coherence metrics that are theoretically principled, parameter-free, and useful to IR.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Lioma, Christina","Tarissan, Fabien","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Petersen, Casper","Larsen, Birger"],"cuid":["S02-093.56-007056"],"event":{"acronym":"ICTIR","end":"2016-09-16","place":"University of Delaware, us","start":"2016-09-12","title":"2016 ACM International Conference on the Theory of Information Retrieval, ICTIR 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","ComUE Paris-Saclay"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploiting the bipartite structure of entity grids for document coherence and retrieval","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84991093535&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-093.56-007056","identifier":[{"id":"84991093535","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9170cca4-c80e-4079-9ad4-58724765d8ad","ku-015e22d5-7755-483d-ad13-026d0627ab03"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1B125083169A6ADAF0BEAB6335CB9361"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The Image Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"comue paris saclay","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"ComUE Paris-Saclay","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Communication and Information Studies (CIS)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"liomapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabien","key":"tarissanpau","last":"Tarissan","name":"Tarissan, Fabien","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Casper","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"b3f33831-f74d-423e-ab97-6e864f3ecc89","name":"Petersen, Casper","orcid":"0000-0001-5858-1985","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birger","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9cb12135-a825-43ba-87e2-b71651b91939","name":"Larsen, Birger","orcid":"0000-0002-3622-2698","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2970398.2970413","eisbn":["9781450344975"],"isbn":["9781450344975"],"pages":"11-20","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"ICTIR 2016 - Proceedings of the 2016 ACM International Conference on the Theory of Information Retrieval"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84991093535"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9170cca4-c80e-4079-9ad4-58724765d8ad","ku-015e22d5-7755-483d-ad13-026d0627ab03"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploiting the Bipartite Structure of Entity Grids for Document Coherence and Retrieval