iliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d168e83a-0358-430e-ba7e-87afc8db95b2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Near optimal adjacency labeling schemes for power-law graphs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-518579","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Shape-changing interfaces allow designers to create user interfaces that physically change shape. However, presently, we lack studies of how such interfaces are designed, as well as what high-level strategies, such as metaphors and affordances, designers use. This paper presents an analysis of sketches made by 21 participants designing either a shape-changing radio or a shapechanging mobile phone. The results exhibit a range of interesting design elements, and the analysis points to a need to further develop or revise existing vocabularies for sketching and analyzing movement. The sketches show a prevalent use of metaphors, say, for communicating volume though big-is-on and small-is-off, as well as a lack of conventions. Furthermore, the affordances used were curiously asymmetrical compared to those offered by nonshapechanging interfaces. We conclude by offering implications on how our results can influence future research on shape-changing interfaces.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Majken Kirkegård","Troiano, Giovanni Maria","Petersen, Marianne Graves","Simonsen, Jakob G.","Hornbæk, Kasper"],"cuid":["S02-086.10-022380"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","end":"2016-05-12","place":"San Jose, us","start":"2016-05-07","title":"34th Annual CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Actuated interfaces","Design","Organic interfaces","Shape changing interfaces"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sketching shape changing interfaces exploring vocabulary metaphors use and affordances","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85015037000","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-086.10-022380","identifier":[{"id":"85015037000","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-854ebc84-1d8c-4554-b295-f08f883d15c4","ku-9c941390-0bf7-482a-aecb-ed2d49103309"],"keyword":["Actuated interfaces","Design","Organic interfaces","Shape-changing interfaces","actuated interfaces, design, organic interfaces, shape-changing interfaces"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2068CB214C6354DE4F7A22325E2968ED"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Engineering, Department of Engineering - Socio-Technical Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The HCC Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Majken Kirkegård","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"a2d4fb12-ea2c-4bd9-b389-d6c4becd13f0","name":"Rasmussen, Majken Kirkegård","orcid":"0000-0003-2530-2331","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Giovanni Maria","key":"troianopau","last":"Troiano","locid":"9639d20c-0be0-4d99-87a0-5071f7d5cc16","name":"Troiano, Giovanni Maria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marianne Graves","key":"petersenpau","la