{"abstract":"We present two novel models of document coherence and their application to information retrieval (IR). Both models approximate document coherence using discourse entities, e.g. the subject or object of a sentence. Our first model views text as a Markov process generating sequences of discourse entities (entity n-grams); we use the entropy of these entity n-grams to approximate the rate at which new information appears in text, reasoning that as more new words appear, the topic increasingly drifts and text coherence decreases. Our second model extends the work of Guinaudeau & Strube [28] that represents text as a graph of discourse entities, linked by different relations, such as their distance or adjacency in text. We use several graph topology metrics to approximate different aspects of the discourse flow that can indicate coherence, such as the average clustering or betweenness of discourse entities in text. Experiments with several instantiations of these models show that: (i) our models perform on a par with two other well-known models of text coherence even without any parameter tuning, and (ii) reranking retrieval results according to their coherence scores gives notable performance gains, confirming a relation between document coherence and relevance. This work contributes two novel models of document coherence, the application of which to IR complements recent work in the integration of document cohesiveness or comprehensibility to ranking [5, 56].","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lioma, Christina","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Larsen, Birger","Hansen, Niels Dalum"],"cuid":["S02-099.73-010425"],"event":{"acronym":"SIGIR","end":"2015-08-13","place":"Santiago de Chile, dk","start":"2015-08-09","title":"International ACM SIGIR Conference on Research and Development in Information Retrieval","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Information retrieval","term dependence"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"non compositional term dependence for information retrieval","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-099.73-010425","identifier":[{"id":"84953807621","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-da48d587-f94a-41b8-ad61-62a3d67e7c7b","ku-e092e25d-92f7-41e1-99c2-d7b0a9713257"],"keyword":["information retrieval","non-compositionality,","term dependence"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B8F8DA44354ECB3781C3236DCD70F0F5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The Image Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Communication and Information Studies (CIS)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"liomapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birger","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9cb12135-a825-43ba-87e2-b71651b91939","name":"Larsen, Birger","orcid":"0000-0002-3622-2698","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels Dalum","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d9d51e53-565c-4597-872e-c43971091313","name":"Hansen, Niels Dalum","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2766462.2767717","eisbn":["9781450336215"],"isbn":["9781450336215"],"pages":"595-604","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 38th International ACM SIGIR Conference on Research and Development in Information Retrieval","title":"SIGIR '15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84953807621"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-da48d587-f94a-41b8-ad61-62a3d67e7c7b","ku-e092e25d-92f7-41e1-99c2-d7b0a9713257"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Non-Compositional Term Dependence for Information Retrieval","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.73-010425","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Users may strive to formulate an adequate textual query for their information need. Search engines assist the users by presenting query suggestions. To preserve the original search intent, suggestions should be context-aware and account for the previous queries issued by the user. Achieving context awareness is challenging due to data sparsity. We present a probabilistic suggestion model that is able to account for sequences of previous queries of arbitrary lengths. Our novel hierarchical recurrent encoder-decoder architecture allows the model to be sensitive to the order of queries in the context while avoiding data sparsity. Additionally, our model can suggest for rare, or long-tail, queries. The produced suggestions are synthetic and are sampled one word at a time, using computationally cheap decoding techniques. This is in contrast to current synthetic suggestion models relying upon machine learning pipelines and hand-engineered feature sets. Results show that it outperforms existing context-aware approaches in a next query prediction setting. In addition to query suggestion, our model is general enough to be used in a variety of other applications.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sordoni, Alessandro","Bengio, Yoshua","Vahabi, Hossein","Lioma, Christina","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Nie, Jian-Yun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-399530"],"event":{"acronym":"CIKM","end":"2015-10-23","place":"Melbourne, au","start":"2015-10-19","title":"CIKM 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Yahoo Inc. (Biz)"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a hierarchical recurrent encoder decoder for generative context aware query suggestion","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/161001019/1507.02221v1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-399530","identifier":[{"id":"84958256008","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0a1d45c8-9ae8-431b-beab-c72ea020daf5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-04D1918DEC44A8A2E9D67B359D261DA3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/161001019/1507.02221v1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/pdf/1507.02221v1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"yahoo inc","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Yahoo Inc. (Biz)","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The Image Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Alessandro","key":"sordonipau","last":"Sordoni","name":"Sordoni, Alessandro","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yoshua","key":"bengiopau","last":"Bengio","name":"Bengio, Yoshua","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hossein","key":"vahabipau","last":"Vahabi","name":"Vahabi, Hossein","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christina","key":"liomapau","last":"Lioma","locid":"f05aae41-ef94-4bb6-8562-8abb5e760f42","name":"Lioma, Christina","orcid":"0000-0003-2600-2701","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jian-Yun","key":"niepau","last":"Nie","name":"Nie, Jian-Yun","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2806416.2806493","eisbn":["9781450337946"],"pages":"553-562","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"CIKM '15 Proceedings of the 24th ACM International on Conference on Information and Knowledge Management"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84958256008"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0a1d45c8-9ae8-431b-beab-c72ea020daf5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A hierarchical recurrent encoder-decoder for generative context-aware query suggestion","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-399530","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"We consider the use of physical and virtual objects having one or more affordances associated to simple interactions with them. Based on Kaptelinin and Nardi’s notion of instrumental affordance, we investigate what it means to break an affordance, and the two ensuing questions we deem most important: how users may (i) achieve their goals in the presence of such broken affordances, and may (ii) repurpose or otherwise interact with artefacts with broken affordances. We argue that (A) thorough analyses of breakdowns of affordances and their associated signifiers and feedbacks have implication for design, particularly so for virtual artefacts, and that (B) there is a largely unexplored design space for designing, and redesigning objects with broken affordances, rather than broken or decayed objects.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Grünbaum, Martin Gielsgaard","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-436608"],"event":{"acronym":"INTERACT","end":"2015-09-18","place":"Bamberg, de","start":"2015-09-14","title":"15th IFIP TC 13 International Conference on Human–Computer Interaction, INTERACT 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Affordances","Breakdown","Design","Mediated action","Technology affordances"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the affordances of broken affordances","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-436608","identifier":[{"id":"84946017932","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-484f1e12-65b1-44e2-ac08-01c2add80676"],"keyword":["Affordances","Breakdown","Design","Mediated action","Technology affordances"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-16183624974C8D9D8B9440D3