{"abstract":"For every real number ß >1, the ß-shift is a dynamical system describing iterations of the map x ¿ ßx mod 1 and is studied intensively in number theory. Each ß-shift has an associated language of finite strings of characters; properties of this language are studied for the additional insight they give into the dynamics of the underlying system. We prove that the language of the ß-shift is recursive iff ß is a computable real number. That fact yields a precise characterization of the reals: The real numbers ß for which we can compute arbitrarily good approximations—hence in particular the numbers for which we can compute their expansion to some base—are precisely those for which there exists a program that decides for any finite sequence of digits whether the sequence occurs as a subword of some element of the ß-shift. While the “only if” part of the proof of the above result is constructive, the “if” part is not. We show that no constructive proof of the “if” part exists. Hence, there exists no algorithm that transforms a program computing arbitrarily good approximations of a real number ß into a program deciding the language of the ß-shift.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-444452"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"beta shifts their languages and computability","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-444452","identifier":[{"id":"78751576094","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5554fcab-5cae-49c6-906f-cfd6b9942365"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-EFF7BE25B7495621A3AEB8B2BA27E090"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00224-009-9245-z","issn":["14324350","14330490"],"issn_org":["14324350"],"issue":"2","journal":"Theory of Computing Systems","pages":"297-318","status":"p","title":"Theory of Computing Systems","volume":"48"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-78751576094"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5554fcab-5cae-49c6-906f-cfd6b9942365"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Beta-shifts, their languages and computability","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-444452","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"We investigate authorship attribution using classifiers based on frame semantics. The purpose is to discover whether adding semantic information to lexical and syntactic methods for authorship attribution will improve them, specifically to address the difficult problem of authorship attribution of translated texts. Our results suggest (i) that frame-based classifiers are usable for author attribution of both translated and untranslated texts; (ii) that framebased classifiers generally perform worse than the baseline classifiers for untranslated texts, but (iii) perform as well as, or superior to the baseline classifiers on translated texts; (iv) that-contrary to current belief-naïve classifiers based on lexical markers may perform tolerably on translated texts if the combination of author and translator is present in the training set of a classifier.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hedegaard, Steffen","Simonsen, Jakob Grue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-480326"],"event":{"end":"2011-06-24","place":"Portland, OR, us","start":"2011-06-19","title":"49th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Human Language Technologies, ACL-HLT 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lost in translation authorship attribution using frame semantics","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84859042203&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-480326","identifier":[{"id":"84859042203","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9166af9e-a9fd-4c57-8277-669a6c41f43f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi