Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anssi","key":"klapuripedh","last":"Klapuri","name":"Klapuri, Anssi","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Colby","key":"leiderpedh","last":"Leider","name":"Leider, Colby","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9780615548654"],"pages":"405-410","publisher":"University of Miami","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 12th International Society for Music Information Retrieval Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84873596832"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ea8a4350-a1f5-4f77-a25e-5d4bac7e237d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Using sequence alignment and voting to improve optical music recognition from multiple recognizers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-533503","year":"2011","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Our goal is to provide a top-down approach to biomolecular computation. In spite of widespread discussion about connections between biology and computation, one question seems notable by its absence: Where are the programs? We identify a number of common features in programming that seem conspicuously absent from the literature on biomolecular computing; to partially redress this absence, we introduce a model of computation that is evidently programmable, by programs reminiscent of low-level computer machine code; and at the same time biologically plausible: its functioning is defined by a single and relatively small set of chemical-like reaction rules. Further properties: the model is stored-program: programs are the same as data, so programs are not only executable, but are also compilable and interpretable. It is universal: all computable functions can be computed (in natural ways and without arcane encodings of data and algorithm); it is also uniform: new ``hardware'' is not needed to solve new problems; and (last but not least) it is Turing complete in a strong sense: a universal algorithm exists, that is able to execute any program, and is not asymptotically inefficient.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hartmann, Lars Røeboe","Jones, Neil","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Vrist, Søren Bjerregaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-457397"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"programming in biomolecular computation programs self interpretation and visualisation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.info.uaic.ro/bin/Annals/Article?v=XXI1&a=9","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-457397","identifier":[{"id":"79960792251","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6b1cc1c6-8609-4881-b805-d97f4e1defd2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-AC2EC4992F4B6BE378682C6C140F1319"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Røeboe","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"938282d9-4473-4e07-a1db-9aa694683ddb","name":"Hartmann, Lars Røeboe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Neil","key":"jonespau","last":"Jones","locid":"d75098fb-0869-4abd-bb9f-6fae75c7296c","name":"Jones, Neil","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Søren Bjerregaard","key":"vristpau","last":"Vrist","name":"Vrist, Søren Bjerregaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["18438121","22482695"],"issn_org":["18438121"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Annals of Computer Science","pages":"73-106","status":"p","title":"Scientific Annals of Computer Science","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79960792251"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6b1cc1c6-8609-4881-b805-d97f4e1defd2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Programming in biomolecular computation : programs, self-interpretation and visualisation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-457397","year":"2011","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Computation via biological devices has been the subject of close scrutiny since von Neumann’s early work some 60 years ago. In spite of the many relevant works in this field, the notion of programming biological devices seems to be, at best, ill-defined. While many devices are claimed or proved to be computationally universal in some sense, the full step to a bona fide programming language is rarely taken, and one question is noticeable by its absence: If the device is universal, where are the programs? We begin with an extensive review of the literature on programming-related biocomputing; and briefly identify some strengths and shortcomings from a programming perspective. To show concretely what one could see as programming in biocomputing, we outline (from recent work) a computation model and a small programming language that are biologically more plausible than existing silicon-inspired models. Whether or not the model is biologically plausible in an absolute sense, we believe it sets a standard for a biological device that can be both universal and programmable.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hartmann, Lars Røeboe","Jones, Neil","Simonsen, Jakob Grue","Vrist, Søren Bjerregaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-460582"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"computational biology a programming perspective","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-460582","identifier":[{"id":"84856596132","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7061145b-3840-437d-b171-aa70ef56af76"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DFF61F9569F506E958CD83FCE77F7E2A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Røeboe","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"938282d9-4473-4e07-a1db-9aa694683ddb","name":"Hartmann, Lars Røeboe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Neil","key":"jonespau","last":"Jones","locid":"d75098fb-0869-4abd-bb9f-6fae75c7296c","name":"Jones, Neil","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Grue","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"833c3e76-0bbe-4624-b1a9-9f0764fa69d0","name":"Simonsen, Jakob Grue","orcid":"0000-0002-3488-9392","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren Bjerregaard","key":"vristpau","last":"Vrist","name":"Vrist, Søren Bjerregaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gul","key":"aghapedh","last":"Agha","name":"Agha, Gul","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Olivier","key":"danvypedh","last":"Danvy","name":"Danvy, Olivier","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"José","key":"meseguerpedh","last":"Meseguer","name":"Meseguer, José","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-24933-4_20","eisbn":["9783642249334"],"isbn":["9783642249327"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"403-433","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture notes in computer science","status":"p","subtitle":"actors, open systems, biological systems","title":"Formal modeling"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84856596132"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid"